exports[`the static pages in en > keeps the privacy policy 1`] = `
"<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Libell privacy policy</title>
<meta name="description" content="Libell is a free open source project. There are no accounts, no ads and no tracking, and nobody collects information about you.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/page.css">
<link rel="icon" href="/icons/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Libell privacy policy</h1>
<p class="changed">Last changed 25 October 2026</p>
<p>Libell is a free open source project. There are no accounts, no ads and no tracking, and nobody collects information about you.</p>
<h2>What is stored on your phone</h2>
<p>Libell stores your vehicles, measurements, settings, calibrations, targets, chosen language and the sensor box you last used. All of it is kept in the browser’s local storage on your phone. It works much like cookies, but it is never sent anywhere. Libell needs it to work, so there is no consent banner.</p>
<p>Under Help › Privacy in the app you can see everything stored and delete all of it. You can also clear the site’s data in your browser.</p>
<h2>Sensors and Bluetooth</h2>
<p>The phone’s motion sensors and Bluetooth are used only on the phone, and only to measure the tilt. The readings never leave the phone.</p>
<h2>Anonymous counting</h2>
<p>To know what to improve, Libell can count its use anonymously with GoatCounter. Libell asks you once whether to count, and nothing is counted until you have chosen. The statistics are public.</p>
<h3>What is counted</h3>
<p>That the app was opened, which features are used, which sensor measures (the phone or a model such as EasyLevel or Xparkle RVS01), the app version and the language chosen in Libell.</p>
<h3>What is never saved</h3>
<p>Your IP address, country, device, screen, operating system or browser, your vehicle’s measurements, your settings, or anything else about you. Only your choice is kept on your phone.</p>
<p>As with any request on the internet, your phone’s IP address and the browser’s name reach GoatCounter. GoatCounter never saves them: it keeps them in memory for at most eight hours to recognise the same visit. GoatCounter is run from Ireland and its servers are in Finland and Germany, so nothing leaves the EU.</p>
<p>You can change your choice any time under Help › Privacy. Offline, nothing is sent and nothing is kept for later. If your browser asks websites not to track you, Libell counts nothing.</p>
<p>The counting rests on your consent under the GDPR (article 6.1 a): you give it with your choice and can take it back at any time. As nothing that identifies you is saved, there is nothing about you to show or delete. You can complain to the data protection authority in your country.</p>
<h2>What you choose to share</h2>
<p>Under Help › Feedback you can open a ready-made issue on GitHub, which you post yourself with your own GitHub account. The issue is public. Besides your text it contains the app version, screen size, time and the browser’s name, and you see all of it before posting.</p>
<p>“Share to another phone” makes a link with the vehicle’s measurements, without calibration. The link goes only where you send it.</p>
<h2>The website</h2>
<p>Libell is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like every web host, GitHub sees your IP address when the page loads. Libell has no access to GitHub’s logs.</p>
<h2>Who is behind Libell</h2>
<p>Libell belongs to its open source project, not to a person or a company. It is free to use however you like under the MIT license, and is provided as is, without warranty.</p>
<h2>Questions and changes</h2>
<p>Ask your questions as an issue on GitHub. When Libell changes what it stores or sends, this page is updated at the same time.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/moggleif/libell/issues">Issues on GitHub</a> · <a href="https://libell.goatcounter.com">See the statistics</a></p>
<p><a href="/">Open Libell</a></p>
<h2>Other languages</h2>
<ul class="languages">
<li><a href="/privacy/ca/" hreflang="ca" lang="ca">Català</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/cs/" hreflang="cs" lang="cs">Čeština</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/da/" hreflang="da" lang="da">Dansk</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/de/" hreflang="de" lang="de">Deutsch</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/et/" hreflang="et" lang="et">Eesti</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/es/" hreflang="es" lang="es">Español</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/fr/" hreflang="fr" lang="fr">Français</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/hr/" hreflang="hr" lang="hr">Hrvatski</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/is/" hreflang="is" lang="is">Íslenska</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/it/" hreflang="it" lang="it">Italiano</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/lv/" hreflang="lv" lang="lv">Latviešu</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/lt/" hreflang="lt" lang="lt">Lietuvių</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/hu/" hreflang="hu" lang="hu">Magyar</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/nl/" hreflang="nl" lang="nl">Nederlands</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/nb/" hreflang="nb" lang="nb">Norsk bokmål</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/pl/" hreflang="pl" lang="pl">Polski</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/pt/" hreflang="pt" lang="pt">Português</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/ro/" hreflang="ro" lang="ro">Română</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/sk/" hreflang="sk" lang="sk">Slovenčina</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/sl/" hreflang="sl" lang="sl">Slovenščina</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/fi/" hreflang="fi" lang="fi">Suomi</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/sv/" hreflang="sv" lang="sv">Svenska</a></li>
<li><a href="/privacy/tr/" hreflang="tr" lang="tr">Türkçe</a></li>
</ul>
</main>
</body>
</html>
"
`;

